Usage: relay <command> [options]

Commands:
  relay status                          The Claude app, the open account and Relay’s state
  relay list                            Saved accounts
  relay add <name>                      Save the Claude app sign-in, or sign in with a new account
  relay switch <name>                   Quit the Claude app and reopen it signed in as <name>
  relay remove <name>                   Forget a saved account
  relay rename <name> <new>             Rename an account
  relay recover                         Restore the backup of an interrupted switch
  relay history [<name>]                Code history sharing; history mode …, history sync
  relay connect <name>                  Sign in to read the account’s usage, or renew it
  relay usage [<name>]                  How much of the 5-hour and weekly limits is used
  relay run <name> [-- …]               Run Claude Code as <name>
  relay tokens                          Daily token usage recorded by Relay.app
  relay proxy [start|status|env]        Local gateway that spreads requests over the accounts (--port, --host)
  relay statusline [install|uninstall]  Account and limits in Claude Code’s status line
  relay doctor                          Check the setup
  relay reset-vault                     Start the sign-in vault over when its Keychain key is lost

Options:
  --yes, -y        Go ahead without asking
  --json           JSON output for read commands
  --lang <code>    Language: en, tr, de, fr, es, pt-BR, it, ja, ko, zh-Hans, zh-Hant, ru, uk, pl, nl
  --no-color       No colors
  --version, -v    Version

Note: commands that quit the Claude app (switch, add, recover, history sync) also stop its Code sessions.
